Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.32,0:00:08.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You performed human transmutation?!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.32,0:00:11.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You've committed that \Nwhich is most sanctioned!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.84,0:00:15.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You've had your bodies \Ntaken over to the other side!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.70,0:00:20.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So this is why your title is "Fullmetal"!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.87,0:00:23.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Fullmetal Alchemist!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.99,0:02:19.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I see, so that's it.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.37,0:02:27.25,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,It's now clear why a kid like you should bear\N the stern-sounding title of "Fullmetal."
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.25,0:02:31.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Rose, alchemy forbids \Nthe transmutation of gold.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.84,0:02:37.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,At the same time, there is one other inherently forbidden practice,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.58,0:02:38.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and that is...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.10,0:02:41.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,human transmutation!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.97,0:02:46.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You miserable, foolish kids!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.08,0:02:49.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You dabbled in human transmutation unaware of its penalties, didn't you?!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:49.98,0:02:51.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No, we didn't! We—
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.50,0:02:52.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:55.36,0:02:58.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We just wanted...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.10,0:03:08.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We just wanted to see our mom's smiling face one more time.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.54,0:03:10.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But you failed!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.66,0:03:17.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah. My brother lost his body, \Nand I lost my left leg and right arm.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.76,0:03:22.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is what happens when two people try to bring a person back to life.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.76,0:03:26.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Rose, this is what it takes to bring someone back to life.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.47,0:03:30.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are you prepared to go through it?!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:34.96,0:03:37.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There is no need for concern.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.00,0:03:41.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I have received this \NPhilosopher's Stone from Leto.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:41.36,0:03:45.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And besides, I am not inexperienced the way they were.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.24,0:03:46.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't be ridiculous!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.70,0:03:49.83,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,No matter what you offer in return, \Nthere are some things that cannot be done!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.83,0:03:53.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then why do you want \Nthe Philosopher's Stone?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.18,0:03:57.52,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,You think that if you had this, you could complete your mom's transmutation, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.52,0:03:59.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You've got it wrong, baldy.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.07,0:04:03.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We just want to get our original bodies back.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.14,0:04:06.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That is, if we {\i1}can{\i0} get them back.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.43,0:04:12.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We'll ask you one more time: \Nplease give us the Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:13.16,0:04:17.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,State Alchemist, may the wrath of God befall you.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.25,0:04:19.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Get down here, third-string,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:19.98,0:04:21.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and I'll show you the difference between our levels!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.85,0:04:30.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wretched fools!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.51,0:04:48.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That was close!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.14,0:04:51.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Minister!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.24,0:04:54.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why, you!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.68,0:04:57.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.96,0:04:59.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This way!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.15,0:05:01.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You fools! There's only one way out!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.98,0:05:03.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If there's no way out...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.28,0:05:06.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll just have to make one!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.41,0:05:10.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:14.62,0:05:16.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,After them!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.58,0:05:18.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Minister...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.50,0:05:20.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That ring...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.53,0:05:23.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are the works of God alchemy?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.78,0:05:29.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Whether or not one calls it alchemy depends on the person.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.10,0:05:33.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,However, what they \Ncannot do, I am able to.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.52,0:05:38.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I've kept you waiting, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.04,0:05:47.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ro...se...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.14,0:05:50.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Cain?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.53,0:05:52.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ro...se...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.37,0:06:02.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Cain has had his spirit first resurrected through the works of Leto.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.56,0:06:06.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,His body should also become complete in a few days.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.30,0:06:09.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Minister...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.18,0:06:12.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is the work of God, isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.12,0:06:22.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If all we wanted to do was \Ntake the Philosopher's Stone,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.32,0:06:24.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,it's not as though we \Ncouldn't have done it.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.95,0:06:32.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This evening, a pair of unbelievers sought the minister's life.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.57,0:06:36.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,One of them is short, and the other is wearing ancient armor.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.79,0:06:43.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Minister asks that the Faithful refrain from venturing outside
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.79,0:06:39.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}Over there!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.43,0:06:42.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}They aren't here.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.00,0:06:44.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}Hey, go check over there!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.16,0:06:46.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,so as not to suffer any harm.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.96,0:07:00.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No question about it, \Nthat's the guy—the short, stranger kid!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.60,0:07:03.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Who are you calling an ultra-hyper-pipsqueak?!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.52,0:07:05.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I never called you that!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.68,0:07:09.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Anyhow, why don't you just simmer down?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.64,0:07:14.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How could you go after \Nthe Minister's life like that?!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.24,0:07:17.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Right! How terrible—a sweet boy like you!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.86,0:07:22.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Listen, his miracles are \Nnothing more than alchemy.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.73,0:07:24.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,By decomposing and restructuring matter—
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.75,0:07:25.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's a lie!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.80,0:07:33.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Moments ago, my boyfriend, Cain, returned to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.72,0:07:36.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's terrific, Rose!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.78,0:07:39.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,After dying in an accident, \NCain has come back to life, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.48,0:07:42.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There, you see? \NIt's not just Rose, either!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.86,0:07:44.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There are many others as well!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.56,0:07:45.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,She's right!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.26,0:07:47.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If that's not a miracle, \Nthen tell me what is!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.64,0:07:50.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Has anyone here actually seen any of those guys?!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.64,0:07:53.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Everyone is said to have left town afterwards—
Dialogue: 0,0:07:53.03,0:07:54.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Silence!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.34,0:08:00.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Th-The statues of Leto!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.16,0:08:01.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's a miracle!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.55,0:08:15.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.78,0:08:45.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Give it back!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.58,0:08:49.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So this is the proof that \Nyou're a State Alchemist, is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.30,0:08:51.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's the first time \NI've seen one of these.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.28,0:08:54.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The reason you can transmute \Nwithout a transmutation circle
Dialogue: 0,0:08:54.58,0:08:58.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,is that this thing works like an amplifier, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.99,0:09:20.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I didn't get any sleep at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:24.56,0:09:26.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The bell's gone!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:38.90,0:09:41.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Feed it to me! My hands are like this, and everything.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:46.44,0:09:47.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Was it really...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.00,0:09:50.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,your boyfriend?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:32.18,0:10:35.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Philosopher's Stone is our secret alone,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.48,0:10:36.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,right?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:48.62,0:10:55.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Cain... I'm sorry. I, um, I just had to talk to you a little...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:56.32,0:10:58.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ro...se...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:05.98,0:11:11.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Minister! Um, I'm terribly sorry about taking the key without permission.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:26.30,0:11:28.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry, Rose.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:28.80,0:11:31.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Even with the power of \Nthe Philosopher's Stone,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:31.22,0:11:34.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,it was all I could do to offer up the lives of the birds to God,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.08,0:11:38.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,in an attempt to replace them \Nwith the life of another, you see.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:39.40,0:11:44.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Perhaps this Chimera, which tweets \Nwith Cain's voice, is not to your liking?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.08,0:11:52.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Give my regards to Cain.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.18,0:11:56.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ro...se...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.25,0:11:58.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ro...se...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:04.98,0:12:09.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There is only one other who knows \Nthe secret of the Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.10,0:12:20.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's dangerous here. Let's go.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:21.50,0:12:22.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Quickly.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:30.10,0:12:33.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Your flim-flamming is going to be found out soon enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.31,0:12:38.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Faithful are not likely to distinguish between alchemy and the works of God.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:38.25,0:12:43.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No, in the sense that it brings \Nhappiness to them, they are the same.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.98,0:12:47.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So then, what's in it for you?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:49.79,0:12:52.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The basic principle of alchemy is equivalent exchange.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.91,0:12:57.42,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,If you're trying to obtain something, you have to pay for it with something of appropriate value.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.42,0:13:00.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,People say that \NBrother is a prodigy at it.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.37,0:13:03.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But it's only because he has paid the price of enough effort...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.12,0:13:07.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,that Brother is who he is now.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:07.90,0:13:11.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You paid the price, didn't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.28,0:13:14.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,An arm, a leg... a whole body...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.34,0:13:16.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and yet now you're \Ntrying to take them back.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:18.15,0:13:20.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And your mother... \NWhat happened to her?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:20.86,0:13:22.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Okay then,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:22.18,0:13:24.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I guess it's time I got started.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:27.40,0:13:30.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So, you're after money, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:30.01,0:13:31.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}Ed?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:30.38,0:13:34.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I can get all the money I want \Nfrom the donations of the Faithful.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:34.25,0:13:40.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What I want are believers who would gladly throw their own lives away for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:40.84,0:13:45.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They believe in resurrection through me \Nand are not afraid to die.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:46.08,0:13:49.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In time, they would become an invincible army.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.34,0:13:55.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Just you watch, in a few years, \NI will set out to tear this country apart!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:58.40,0:14:00.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Makes no difference to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.42,0:14:01.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What?!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:01.54,0:14:06.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,After all, you can't really bring anyone back to life, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.74,0:14:09.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Of course not! Even if I used the Philosopher's Stone,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:09.68,0:14:13.02,Dialogue,,20,20,0,,there's no telling what would happen if I performed human transmutation.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:13.02,0:14:17.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why, for the sake of the Faithful, \Nwho are nothing more than my pawns...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:17.40,0:14:19.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,would I run the risk of...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:24.84,0:14:25.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wha—
Dialogue: 0,0:14:25.96,0:14:28.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\t(1110,1360,\alpha&HFF&)\t(1360,1610,\1a&H00&,\3a&H00&,\4a&B4&)\t(2260,2760,\alpha&HFF&)}What?!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.22,0:14:32.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How long?! How long \Nhas that mic been on?!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.72,0:14:34.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,For the whole time \Nyou've been here.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:34.84,0:14:37.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How... How did you get my broadcast equipment?!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:37.75,0:14:39.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That was my brother.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.48,0:14:44.44,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,Ah, what got busted up yesterday was just \Nsome junk that I transmuted to look like him.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.44,0:14:46.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No! It's all a lie!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:47.00,0:14:48.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You must not believe it!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:59.75,0:15:02.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Like I said, I'm on \Na whole different level!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:19.94,0:15:23.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Minister, was that broadcast just now for real?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.90,0:15:32.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I do not know what the heretic has broadcast in my voice,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:32.25,0:15:34.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but it was all a conspiracy!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:34.40,0:15:38.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,As a testament to this, I will eradicate the heretic by the power of God!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.55,0:15:42.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is the power of God!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:51.70,0:15:52.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's a miracle!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.60,0:15:54.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The statues of Leto...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.52,0:15:59.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Give it up, would you?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:00.45,0:16:06.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Without this, you're limited to transmuting your own Automail, aren't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:06.23,0:16:10.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Pops, I'm about to show you the {\i1}real{\i0} hammer of God!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:31.38,0:16:32.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Impossible!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.68,0:16:36.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Not even with the Philosopher's Stone could something so gigantic be moved!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:39.18,0:16:44.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The watch has nothing to do with it. Brother is the Fullmetal Alchemist!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.45,0:17:15.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I won't let you have it! I won't let you have the Philosopher's Stone!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.56,0:17:27.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Rebound?!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:38.36,0:17:40.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,An imitation?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:42.62,0:17:44.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,After all the commotion you've raised...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:44.90,0:17:48.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,After all the trouble you put me through, it was a fake?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.20,0:17:53.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Stop jerking me around!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:01.60,0:18:03.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That was quite a wild goose chase, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.88,0:18:07.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And here I thought we were finally \Ngoing to be able to restore your body.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.52,0:18:10.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You should come first, Brother.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.30,0:18:13.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That Automail is so hard on you, and all...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:13.27,0:18:16.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nothing more to do \Nbut to keep searching, I guess.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:17.74,0:18:20.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How could you do that to us?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:20.55,0:18:24.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,To us, the Minister's miracles gave us hope.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:24.85,0:18:29.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If we believed, even dead people could come back to life.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:29.00,0:18:32.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That was the only hope we had!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:33.60,0:18:36.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're saying we should have \Nleft everything the way it was?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:37.42,0:18:42.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What am I supposed to cling to \Nas I continue living from now on?!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:43.46,0:18:44.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Tell me!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.84,0:18:51.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You'll have to decide that for yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:51.32,0:18:54.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Get up and walk. Move forward.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.78,0:18:58.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You've got some fine legs there, \Ndon't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:10.52,0:19:13.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I think Brother did all this for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.40,0:19:16.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He shouldn't have bothered!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:17.14,0:19:20.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We've seen all sorts of things.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.70,0:19:28.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How can this be?!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:28.18,0:19:32.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That thing you gave me wasn't the real Philosopher's Stone?!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.62,0:19:36.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Of course not. \NThis city is just a decoy, after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.58,0:19:42.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Those who hear the stories about \Nthe Philosopher's Stone gather here,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:42.75,0:19:44.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and then...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:44.32,0:19:47.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wh-Who are you guys? Why are you here?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:48.08,0:19:51.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lust, is it okay \Nif I eat this old man?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:01.72,0:20:03.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Where did that miserable Cornello run away to?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:03.61,0:20:05.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That rotten false minister!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:08.74,0:20:10.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What is all this?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:10.05,0:20:11.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What went on here?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:11.51,0:20:12.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is awful...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:16.34,0:20:18.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Minister?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:28.92,0:20:30.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's a miracle...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:30.13,0:20:31.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're sure it's not just another trick?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:31.98,0:20:33.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But they came back to life!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:34.22,0:20:38.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It seems that the Devil worked wickedness in my absence.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:38.12,0:20:39.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is everyone all right?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:40.90,0:20:44.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're the real... \Nthe real minister, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:47.36,0:20:49.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Cornello-sama!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:49.12,0:20:51.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We were deceived by that kid!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:51.12,0:20:52.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's right!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:55.94,0:21:00.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Envy, I'm sorry, but we must ask you to keep that form for a little while.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:08.86,0:21:12.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We've seen all sorts of things.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:12.30,0:21:14.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm going to tell you about them.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:14.52,0:21:18.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You must not come down the same path as us.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:18.64,0:21:20.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's what I believe.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:25.30,0:21:32.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We were born and raised in a small village east of Central named Resembool.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:33.22,0:21:35.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's where everything began.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:38.60,0:21:39.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mom!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:39.69,0:21:41.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mom, look, look!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:43.57,0:21:45.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,See?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:45.07,0:21:46.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, my!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:46.16,0:21:48.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother made it!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:48.38,0:21:50.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I can still only do this.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:52.01,0:21:54.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Incredible, both of you!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:54.32,0:21:56.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You certainly are his children!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:01.42,0:22:06.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Man cannot obtain anything \Nwithout first sacrificing something.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:07.10,0:22:11.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In order to obtain anything, \Nsomething of equal value is required.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:11.92,0:22:16.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That is alchemy's \NLaw of Equivalent Exchange.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:17.80,0:22:23.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,At the time, we believed that \Nto be the true way of the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:38.75,0:23:40.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Fullmetal Alchemist{\i0}...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:40.34,0:23:42.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Episode 3: "Mother..."
Dialogue: 0,0:23:42.98,0:23:45.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I loved Mom's lullabies.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:45.96,0:23:50.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mom's stew tasted like milk, but Brother loved it.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:50.56,0:23:52.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's why we had to...
